-- ccc22-indictments.l4 -- sections 574 to 580 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XX: preferring
-- indictments, direct indictments, summons or warrant on an indictment, stay of proceedings by the Attorney General,
-- intervention by the Attorney General of Canada, form of indictment). Part agent ccc22. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to
-- 2026-09-30). It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (the text's own words bring the case within the rule); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words);
-- NOTHING (not covered). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. See NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc22)".
-- Tags in the comments: [M-a] a failed "if"/"where" or a flat negative counted as the text's no; [M-b] a prohibition or grant limited by its
-- own wording counted as NOT the text's no (NOTHING); [F:...] a fork line for NOTES.md (may-if, may-where, entitled, duty, unless).
-- Section 2 terms and other parts' answers are INPUTS named for their section (PLAN.md section 4).

§ `Section 574 -- Prosecutor may prefer indictment`

-- (1): the prosecutor may prefer an indictment against a person ordered to stand trial, on (a) a charge on which they were ordered to stand trial or
-- (b) a charge founded on the facts disclosed by the evidence at the preliminary inquiry. "Subject to subsection (3)" is the composition at the end of this section.
-- src:12534 | 574 (1) Subject to subsection (3), the prosecutor may, whether the charges were included in one information or not, prefer an indictment against any person who has been ordered to stand trial in respect of
-- src:12535 | (a) any charge on which that person was ordered to stand trial; or
-- src:12536 | (b) any charge founded on the facts disclosed by the evidence taken on the preliminary inquiry, in addition to or in substitution for any charge on which that person was ordered to stand trial.
@ref s 574(1) (src:12534-12536)
GIVEN `s 548 the decision the justice made at the preliminary inquiry` IS A `Decision on the charge`
      `the charge is one on which the person was ordered to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is founded on the facts disclosed by the evidence taken on the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 574(1) the prosecutor may prefer an indictment against a person ordered to stand trial` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 548 the decision the justice made at the preliminary inquiry` EQUALS `an order to stand trial`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who has been ordered to stand trial"
        IF `the charge is one on which the person was ordered to stand trial` OR `the charge is founded on the facts disclosed by the evidence taken on the preliminary inquiry` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "(a) any charge on which that person was ordered to stand trial; or (b) any charge founded on the facts disclosed by the evidence"

-- (1.1): no preliminary inquiry requested, or none available: the prosecutor may prefer an indictment on a charge in an information (or an included charge) at any time after the person has made an election, re-election or deemed election.
-- src:12538 | (1.1) If a person has not requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4) or 536.1(3) into the charge or was not entitled to make such a request, the prosecutor may, subject to subsection (3), prefer an indictment against a person in respect of a charge set out in an information or informations, or any included charge, at any time after the person has made an election, re-election or deemed election on the information or informations.
@ref s 574(1.1) (src:12538-12538)
GIVEN `the person has requested a preliminary inquiry into the charge under subsection 536(4) or 536.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was entitled to make such a request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is set out in the information or informations, or is an included charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has made an election, re-election or deemed election on the information or informations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 574(1.1) the prosecutor may prefer an indictment where no preliminary inquiry was requested` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has requested a preliminary inquiry into the charge under subsection 536(4) or 536.1(3)` AND `the person was entitled to make such a request` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person has not requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4) or 536.1(3) into the charge or was not entitled to make such a request" [F:may-if]
        IF NOT `the charge is set out in the information or informations, or is an included charge` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a charge set out in an information or informations, or any included charge"
        IF NOT `the person has made an election, re-election or deemed election on the information or informations` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time after the person has made an election, re-election or deemed election" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling (a) of 2026-11-05, so the answer is JUST FALSE outside it) [F:may-where] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (1.2): a single indictment combining charges under (1) and (1.1). The inputs are the answers of the two functions above.
-- src:12540 | (1.2) If indictments may be preferred under both subsections (1) and (1.1), the prosecutor may prefer a single indictment in respect of one or more charges referred to in subsection (1) combined with one or more charges or included charges referred to in subsection (1.1).
@ref s 574(1.2) (src:12540-12540)
GIVEN `the answer of s 574(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 574(1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 574(1.2) the prosecutor may prefer a single indictment under both subsections` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 574(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the answer of s 574(1.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If indictments may be preferred under both subsections (1) and (1.1)" [F:may-if]

-- (2): the indictment may, if the accused consents, include a charge not referred to in subsections (1) to (1.2).
-- src:12542 | (2) An indictment preferred under any of subsections (1) to (1.2) may, if the accused consents, include a charge that is not referred to in those subsections, and the offence charged may be dealt with, tried and determined and punished in all respects as if it were an offence in respect of which the accused had been ordered to stand trial. However, if the offence was committed wholly in a province other than that in which the accused is before the court, subsection 478(3) applies.
@ref s 574(2) (src:12542-12542)
GIVEN `the indictment was preferred under one of subsections (1) to (1.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 574(2) the indictment may include a charge not referred to in subsections (1) to (1.2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the indictment was preferred under one of subsections (1) to (1.2)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An indictment preferred under any of subsections (1) to (1.2)"
        IF NOT `the accused consents` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the accused consents" [F:may-if]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2), last sentence: "However, if the offence was committed wholly in a province other than that in which the accused is before the court, subsection 478(3) applies."
-- src:12542 | (2) An indictment preferred under any of subsections (1) to (1.2) may, if the accused consents, include a charge that is not referred to in those subsections, and the offence charged may be dealt with, tried and determined and punished in all respects as if it were an offence in respect of which the accused had been ordered to stand trial. However, if the offence was committed wholly in a province other than that in which the accused is before the court, subsection 478(3) applies.
@ref s 574(2) (src:12542-12542)
GIVEN `the offence was committed wholly in a province other than that in which the accused is before the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
