-- (3): a private prosecution needs the written order of a judge of that court. The answer is the BAR: JUST TRUE where the section bars preferring the indictment.
-- src:12544 | (3) In a prosecution conducted by a prosecutor other than the Attorney General and in which the Attorney General does not intervene, an indictment may not be preferred under any of subsections (1) to (1.2) before a court without the written order of a judge of that court.
