§ `Section 576 -- Indictment`

-- (1) "Except as provided in this Act, no indictment shall be preferred." The answer is the BAR.
-- src:12547 | 576 (1) Except as provided in this Act, no indictment shall be preferred.
@ref s 576(1) (src:12547-12547)
GIVEN `this Act provides for preferring the indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 576(1) the section bars preferring the indictment` MEANS
    IF `this Act provides for preferring the indictment`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as provided in this Act, no indictment shall be preferred" [F:unless] [M-a]
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2) "No criminal information shall be laid or granted and no bill of indictment shall be preferred before a grand jury."
-- src:12549 | (2) No criminal information shall be laid or granted and no bill of indictment shall be preferred before a grand jury.
@ref s 576(2) (src:12549-12549)
GIVEN `the step is a criminal information laid or granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the step is a bill of indictment preferred before a grand jury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 576(2) the section bars a criminal information or a bill of indictment before a grand jury` MEANS
    IF `the step is a criminal information laid or granted` OR `the step is a bill of indictment preferred before a grand jury`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names two steps and says nothing of any other

-- (3) "No person shall be tried on a coroner’s inquisition."
-- src:12551 | (3) No person shall be tried on a coroner’s inquisition.
@ref s 576(3) (src:12551-12551)
GIVEN `the person is to be tried on a coroner’s inquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 576(3) the section bars trying a person on a coroner’s inquisition` MEANS
    IF `the person is to be tried on a coroner’s inquisition`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names one way of trying a person and says nothing of any other

§ `Section 577 -- Direct indictments`

-- Where the accused is, at the time a direct indictment is preferred. The three situations of the opening words, and "none of those".
-- src:12553 | 577 Despite section 574, an indictment may be preferred even if the accused has not been given the opportunity to request a preliminary inquiry, a preliminary inquiry has been commenced but not concluded or a preliminary inquiry has been held and the accused has been discharged, if
@ref s 577 (the situations) (src:12553-12553)
DECLARE `s 577 where the accused is in the preliminary-inquiry process` IS ONE OF
    `s 577 the accused has not been given the opportunity to request a preliminary inquiry`
    `s 577 a preliminary inquiry has been commenced but not concluded`
    `s 577 a preliminary inquiry has been held and the accused has been discharged`
    `s 577 none of those situations`

-- 577: "Despite section 574, an indictment may be preferred even if [situation], if (a) ... the personal consent in writing of the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General is filed in court; or (b) in any other case, a judge of the court so orders."
-- This is the answer ccc21 (ss 536, 536.1, 561, 561.1) takes as its input `s 577 a direct indictment has been preferred` (PLAN.md section 6, seam).
-- src:12553 | 577 Despite section 574, an indictment may be preferred even if the accused has not been given the opportunity to request a preliminary inquiry, a preliminary inquiry has been commenced but not concluded or a preliminary inquiry has been held and the accused has been discharged, if
-- src:12554 | (a) in the case of a prosecution conducted by the Attorney General or one in which the Attorney General intervenes, the personal consent in writing of the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General is filed in court; or
-- src:12555 | (b) in any other case, a judge of the court so orders.
@ref s 577 (src:12553-12555)
GIVEN `an indictment has been preferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      situation IS A `s 577 where the accused is in the preliminary-inquiry process`
      `the prosecution is conducted by the Attorney General or is one in which the Attorney General intervenes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal consent in writing of the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General is filed in court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a judge of the court so orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 577 a direct indictment has been preferred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an indictment has been preferred` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section speaks only of an indictment that is preferred
        IF situation EQUALS `s 577 none of those situations` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "even if the accused has not been given the opportunity to request a preliminary inquiry, a preliminary inquiry has been commenced but not concluded or a preliminary inquiry has been held and the accused has been discharged"
        IF `the prosecution is conducted by the Attorney General or is one in which the Attorney General intervenes` THEN
            (IF `the personal consent in writing of the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General is filed in court` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) in the case of a prosecution conducted by the Attorney General or one in which the Attorney General intervenes, the personal consent in writing of the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General is filed in court" [M-a]
        OTHERWISE (IF `a judge of the court so orders` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in any other case, a judge of the court so orders" [M-a]

§ `Section 578 -- Summons or warrant`

-- (1): where notice of recommencement has been given under 579(2), or an indictment has been filed with the court, the court, if it considers it necessary, may issue a summons or a warrant for the arrest of the accused to compel attendance.
-- src:12557 | 578 (1) Where notice of the recommencement of proceedings has been given pursuant to subsection 579(2) or an indictment has been filed with the court before which the proceedings are to commence or recommence, the court, if it considers it necessary, may issue
-- src:12558 | (a) a summons addressed to, or
-- src:12559 | (b) a warrant for the arrest of,
-- src:12560 | the accused or defendant, as the case may be, to compel him to attend before the court to answer the charge described in the indictment.
@ref s 578(1) (src:12557-12560)
GIVEN `notice of the recommencement of proceedings has been given under subsection 579(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an indictment has been filed with the court before which the proceedings are to commence or recommence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      process IS A `Process document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 578(1) the court may issue a summons or a warrant for the arrest of the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`notice of the recommencement of proceedings has been given under subsection 579(2)` OR `an indictment has been filed with the court before which the proceedings are to commence or recommence`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where notice of the recommencement of proceedings has been given pursuant to subsection 579(2) or an indictment has been filed with the court" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF NOT `the court considers it necessary` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court, if it considers it necessary, may issue" [F:may-if]
        IF process EQUALS `a summons` OR process EQUALS `a warrant for arrest` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may issue (a) a summons ... or (b) a warrant for the arrest of" names two documents and does not say "only"

-- (2): Part XVI applies with such modifications as the circumstances require where a summons or warrant is issued under (1).
-- src:12561 | Part XVI to apply
-- src:12562 | (2) The provisions of Part XVI apply with such modifications as the circumstances require where a summons or warrant is issued under subsection (1).
@ref s 578(2) (src:12561-12562)
GIVEN `a summons or warrant is issued under subsection 578(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 578(2) Part XVI applies` MEANS
    IF `a summons or warrant is issued under subsection 578(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a summons or warrant is issued under subsection (1)" [M-a]

§ `Section 579 -- Attorney General may direct stay`

-- (1): the Attorney General (or counsel instructed for the purpose) may, at any time after proceedings are commenced and before judgment, direct the clerk to enter a stay.
-- src:12564 | 579 (1) The Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for that purpose may, at any time after any proceedings in relation to an accused or a defendant are commenced and before judgment, direct the clerk or other proper officer of the court to make an entry on the record that the proceedings are stayed by the Attorney General’s or counsel’s direction, as the case may be, and the entry shall then be made, at which time the proceedings shall be stayed accordingly and any undertaking or release order relating to the proceedings is vacated.
@ref s 579(1) (src:12564-12564)
GIVEN `the person directing is the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings in relation to an accused or a defendant have been commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `judgment has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579(1) the Attorney General may direct the clerk to enter a stay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person directing is the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for that purpose` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for that purpose may"
        IF (NOT `proceedings in relation to an accused or a defendant have been commenced`) OR `judgment has been given` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time after any proceedings in relation to an accused or a defendant are commenced and before judgment" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling (a) of 2026-11-05) [F:may-where] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (1), the effect: once the entry is made the proceedings are stayed and any undertaking or release order relating to them is vacated.
-- src:12564 | 579 (1) The Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for that purpose may, at any time after any proceedings in relation to an accused or a defendant are commenced and before judgment, direct the clerk or other proper officer of the court to make an entry on the record that the proceedings are stayed by the Attorney General’s or counsel’s direction, as the case may be, and the entry shall then be made, at which time the proceedings shall be stayed accordingly and any undertaking or release order relating to the proceedings is vacated.
@ref s 579(1) (src:12564-12564)
GIVEN `the answer of s 579(1) the Attorney General may direct the clerk to enter a stay` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the entry has been made on the record that the proceedings are stayed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579(1) the proceedings are stayed and any undertaking or release order relating to them is vacated` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the entry has been made on the record that the proceedings are stayed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the entry shall then be made, at which time the proceedings shall be stayed accordingly" (no entry, no stay yet) [M-a]
        IF `the answer of s 579(1) the Attorney General may direct the clerk to enter a stay` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the direction was one the subsection authorizes is the answer of the function above

-- (2): stayed proceedings may be recommenced without a new information or indictment by notice to the clerk; where no notice is given within one year after the entry of the stay,
-- or before the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires, whichever is the earlier, they are deemed never to have been commenced.
-- src:12566 | (2) Proceedings stayed in accordance with subsection (1) may be recommenced, without laying a new information or preferring a new indictment, as the case may be, by the Attorney General or counsel instructed by him for that purpose giving notice of the recommencement to the clerk of the court in which the stay of the proceedings was entered, but where no such notice is given within one year after the entry of the stay of proceedings, or before the expiration of the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced, whichever is the earlier, the proceedings shall be deemed never to have been commenced.
@ref s 579(2) (src:12566-12566)
GIVEN `the proceedings were stayed in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General has given notice of the recommencement to the clerk of the court in which the stay was entered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579(2) the stayed proceedings may be recommenced without laying a new information or preferring a new indictment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings were stayed in accordance with subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Proceedings stayed in accordance with subsection (1)"
        IF NOT `the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General has given notice of the recommencement to the clerk of the court in which the stay was entered` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by the Attorney General or counsel instructed by him for that purpose giving notice of the recommencement to the clerk of the court" [F:may-if]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The last day for the notice under (2): the earlier of the first anniversary of the entry of the stay and the expiry of the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced
-- (that expiry is for another provision and is an input). "Within one year after the entry" is read as including the anniversary itself, as section 579.001(4) says in terms ("on or before the first anniversary").
-- src:12566 | (2) Proceedings stayed in accordance with subsection (1) may be recommenced, without laying a new information or preferring a new indictment, as the case may be, by the Attorney General or counsel instructed by him for that purpose giving notice of the recommencement to the clerk of the court in which the stay of the proceedings was entered, but where no such notice is given within one year after the entry of the stay of proceedings, or before the expiration of the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced, whichever is the earlier, the proceedings shall be deemed never to have been commenced.
@ref s 579(2) (src:12566-12566)
GIVEN `the day the stay was entered` IS A DATE
      `the day the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 579(2) the last day for the notice of recommencement` MEANS
    IF `add years` `the day the stay was entered` 1 AT MOST `the day the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires`
    THEN `add years` `the day the stay was entered` 1
    ELSE `the day the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires`

-- src:12566 | (2) Proceedings stayed in accordance with subsection (1) may be recommenced, without laying a new information or preferring a new indictment, as the case may be, by the Attorney General or counsel instructed by him for that purpose giving notice of the recommencement to the clerk of the court in which the stay of the proceedings was entered, but where no such notice is given within one year after the entry of the stay of proceedings, or before the expiration of the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced, whichever is the earlier, the proceedings shall be deemed never to have been commenced.
@ref s 579(2) (src:12566-12566)
GIVEN `the day the stay was entered` IS A DATE
      `the day the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579(2) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the notice was given`
    WHEN JUST given THEN
        (IF given AT MOST `s 579(2) the last day for the notice of recommencement` `the day the stay was entered` `the day the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where no such notice is given within one year after the entry of the stay of proceedings, or before the expiration of the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced, whichever is the earlier" (notice was given in time) [M-a]
         ELSE JUST TRUE)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        (IF `the day asked about` GREATER THAN `s 579(2) the last day for the notice of recommencement` `the day the stay was entered` `the day the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the last day for notice has not passed, so the section does not yet say the proceedings are deemed never commenced

-- (2), the regulative twin: the Attorney General may give notice of recommencement within the period; HENCE the proceedings may be recommenced, LEST (no notice in time) they are deemed never commenced.
-- The period is counted in days by this file's convention (the number of days from the entry of the stay to the last day); the decision functions above are the calendar rule.
-- src:12566 | (2) Proceedings stayed in accordance with subsection (1) may be recommenced, without laying a new information or preferring a new indictment, as the case may be, by the Attorney General or counsel instructed by him for that purpose giving notice of the recommencement to the clerk of the court in which the stay of the proceedings was entered, but where no such notice is given within one year after the entry of the stay of proceedings, or before the expiration of the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced, whichever is the earlier, the proceedings shall be deemed never to have been commenced.
@ref s 579(2) (src:12566-12566)
DECLARE `s 579(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 579(2) give notice of the recommencement to the clerk of the court`

@ref s 579(2) (src:12566-12566)
GIVEN `the number of days from the entry of the stay to the last day for the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 579(2) action`
`s 579(2) the Attorney General may recommence the stayed proceedings by notice` MEANS
    PARTY `the Attorney General`
    MAY `s 579(2) give notice of the recommencement to the clerk of the court`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the entry of the stay to the last day for the notice`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- No LEST: a MAY that lapses has no consequence for the party (stable 1.6.110 ignores a LEST after MAY: dialects.md, "A MAY with an explicit LEST"); the text's consequence of a lapse
    -- ("the proceedings shall be deemed never to have been commenced") is a legal effect, not a breach, and is the function `s 579(2) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced`.

§ `Section 579.001 -- Instruction to stay (preclearance officers)`

-- (1): the Attorney General shall, after proceedings about an act or omission of a preclearance officer (Preclearance Act, 2016, s 5) are commenced and before judgment, direct the clerk to enter a stay, if the United States has given notice of the exercise of primary criminal jurisdiction.
-- src:12568 | 579.001 (1) The Attorney General or counsel instructed by him or her for that purpose shall, at any time after proceedings in relation to an act or omission of a preclearance officer, as defined in section 5 of the Preclearance Act, 2016, are commenced and before judgment, direct the clerk or other proper officer of the court to make an entry on the record that the proceedings are stayed by direction of the Attorney General if the Government of the United States has provided notice of the exercise of primary criminal jurisdiction under paragraph 14 of Article X of the Agreement.
@ref s 579.001(1) (src:12568-12568)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in relation to an act or omission of a preclearance officer, as defined in section 5 of the Preclearance Act, 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings have been commenced and judgment has not been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Government of the United States has provided notice of the exercise of primary criminal jurisdiction under paragraph 14 of Article X of the Agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579.001(1) the Attorney General must direct the clerk to enter a stay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are in relation to an act or omission of a preclearance officer, as defined in section 5 of the Preclearance Act, 2016` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "proceedings in relation to an act or omission of a preclearance officer, as defined in section 5 of the Preclearance Act, 2016"
        IF NOT `the proceedings have been commenced and judgment has not been given` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time after proceedings in relation to an act or omission of a preclearance officer, as defined in section 5 of the Preclearance Act, 2016, are commenced and before judgment" [M-a] [F:duty]
        IF NOT `the Government of the United States has provided notice of the exercise of primary criminal jurisdiction under paragraph 14 of Article X of the Agreement` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Government of the United States has provided notice of the exercise of primary criminal jurisdiction under paragraph 14 of Article X of the Agreement" [M-a] [F:duty]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2): the clerk shall make the entry immediately after being so directed; on the entry being made the proceedings are stayed and any recognizance relating to them is vacated.
-- src:12570 | (2) The clerk or other officer of the court shall make the entry immediately after being so directed, and on the entry being made the proceedings are stayed and any recognizance relating to the proceedings is vacated.
@ref s 579.001(2) (src:12570-12570)
GIVEN `the entry has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579.001(2) the proceedings are stayed and any recognizance relating to them is vacated` MEANS
    IF `the entry has been made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the entry being made the proceedings are stayed" (no entry, no stay yet) [M-a]

-- src:12570 | (2) The clerk or other officer of the court shall make the entry immediately after being so directed, and on the entry being made the proceedings are stayed and any recognizance relating to the proceedings is vacated.
@ref s 579.001(2) (src:12570-12570)
DECLARE `s 579.001(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 579.001(2) make the entry that the proceedings are stayed`

@ref s 579.001(2) (src:12570-12570)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 579.001(2) action`
`s 579.001(2) the clerk must make the entry immediately` MEANS
    PARTY `the clerk of the court`
    MUST `s 579.001(2) make the entry that the proceedings are stayed`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the entry was not made immediately after the clerk was directed"

-- (3): the proceedings may be recommenced without a new information or indictment if the Attorney General gives notice to the clerk that (a) the United States has given notice of waiver (paragraph 15 of Article X) or (b) the United States has declined, or is unable, to prosecute and the accused has returned to Canada.
-- src:12572 | (3) The proceedings may be recommenced without laying a new information or preferring a new indictment, if the Attorney General or counsel instructed by him or her gives notice to the clerk or other officer of the court that
-- src:12573 | (a) the Government of the United States has provided notice of waiver under paragraph 15 of Article X of the Agreement; or
-- src:12574 | (b) the Government of the United States has declined, or is unable, to prosecute the accused and the accused has returned to Canada.
@ref s 579.001(3) (src:12572-12574)
GIVEN `the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General has given notice to the clerk or other officer of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice says that the Government of the United States has provided notice of waiver under paragraph 15 of Article X of the Agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice says that the Government of the United States has declined, or is unable, to prosecute the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice says that the accused has returned to Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579.001(3) the proceedings may be recommenced without laying a new information or preferring a new indictment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General has given notice to the clerk or other officer of the court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Attorney General or counsel instructed by him or her gives notice to the clerk or other officer of the court that" [F:may-if]
        IF `the notice says that the Government of the United States has provided notice of waiver under paragraph 15 of Article X of the Agreement` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the notice says that the Government of the United States has declined, or is unable, to prosecute the accused` AND `the notice says that the accused has returned to Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) the Government of the United States has provided notice of waiver ...; or (b) the Government of the United States has declined, or is unable, to prosecute the accused and the accused has returned to Canada" [F:may-if]

-- (4): however, if the Attorney General does not give notice under (3) on or before the first anniversary of the day on which the stay was entered, the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced.
-- src:12575 | Proceedings deemed never commenced
-- src:12576 | (4) However, if the Attorney General or counsel does not give notice under subsection (3) on or before the first anniversary of the day on which the stay of proceedings was entered, the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced.
@ref s 579.001(4) (src:12575-12576)
GIVEN `the day the stay was entered` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice under subsection (3) was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579.001(4) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the notice under subsection (3) was given`
    WHEN JUST given THEN
        (IF given AT MOST `add years` `the day the stay was entered` 1
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Attorney General or counsel does not give notice under subsection (3) on or before the first anniversary of the day on which the stay of proceedings was entered" (notice was given in time) [M-a]
         ELSE JUST TRUE)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        (IF `the day asked about` GREATER THAN `add years` `the day the stay was entered` 1
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the first anniversary has not passed, so the subsection does not yet say the proceedings are deemed never commenced

-- (5): "In this section, Agreement means the Agreement on Land, Rail, Marine, and Air Transport Preclearance between the Government of Canada and the Government of the United States of America, done at Washington on March 16, 2015."
-- src:12578 | (5) In this section, Agreement means the Agreement on Land, Rail, Marine, and Air Transport Preclearance between the Government of Canada and the Government of the United States of America, done at Washington on March 16, 2015.
@ref s 579.001(5) (src:12578-12578)
GIVEN title IS A STRING
      `the parties` IS A STRING
      `the place it was done` IS A STRING
      `the day it was done` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 579.001(5) the instrument is the Agreement` MEANS
        title EQUALS "Agreement on Land, Rail, Marine, and Air Transport Preclearance"
    AND `the parties` EQUALS "the Government of Canada and the Government of the United States of America"
    AND `the place it was done` EQUALS "Washington"
    AND `the day it was done` EQUALS Date 16 3 2015

§ `Section 579.01 -- When Attorney General does not stay proceedings`

-- src:12580 | 579.01 If the Attorney General intervenes in proceedings and does not stay them under section 579, he or she may, without conducting the proceedings, call witnesses, examine and cross-examine witnesses, present evidence and make submissions.
@ref s 579.01 (src:12580-12580)
DECLARE `s 579.01 step the Attorney General takes without conducting the proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `s 579.01 call witnesses`
    `s 579.01 examine and cross-examine witnesses`
    `s 579.01 present evidence`
    `s 579.01 make submissions`
    `s 579.01 some other step`

-- src:12580 | 579.01 If the Attorney General intervenes in proceedings and does not stay them under section 579, he or she may, without conducting the proceedings, call witnesses, examine and cross-examine witnesses, present evidence and make submissions.
@ref s 579.01 (src:12580-12580)
GIVEN `the Attorney General intervenes in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General has stayed the proceedings under section 579` IS A BOOLEAN
      step IS A `s 579.01 step the Attorney General takes without conducting the proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579.01 the Attorney General may take the step without conducting the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Attorney General intervenes in the proceedings`) OR `the Attorney General has stayed the proceedings under section 579` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Attorney General intervenes in proceedings and does not stay them under section 579" [F:may-if]
        IF step EQUALS `s 579.01 some other step` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "he or she may, without conducting the proceedings, call witnesses, examine and cross-examine witnesses, present evidence and make submissions"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 579.1 -- Intervention by Attorney General of Canada or Director of Public Prosecutions`

-- (1): may intervene in the following circumstances: (a) an offence for which he or she has the power to commence or conduct a proceeding; (b) not instituted by an Attorney General; (c) judgment not rendered; (d) the provincial Attorney General has not intervened.
-- src:12582 | 579.1 (1) The Attorney General of Canada or the Director of Public Prosecutions appointed under subsection 3(1) of the Director of Public Prosecutions Act, or counsel instructed by him or her for that purpose, may intervene in proceedings in the following circumstances:
-- src:12583 | (a) the proceedings are in respect of an offence for which he or she has the power to commence or to conduct a proceeding;
-- src:12584 | (b) the proceedings have not been instituted by an Attorney General;
-- src:12585 | (c) judgment has not been rendered; and
-- src:12586 | (d) the Attorney General of the province in which the proceedings are taken has not intervened.
@ref s 579.1(1) (src:12582-12586)
GIVEN `the person is the Attorney General of Canada, the Director of Public Prosecutions or counsel instructed by either for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in respect of an offence for which he or she has the power to commence or to conduct a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings have not been instituted by an Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `judgment has not been rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of the province in which the proceedings are taken has not intervened` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579.1(1) the Attorney General of Canada or the Director of Public Prosecutions may intervene` MEANS
    IF     `the person is the Attorney General of Canada, the Director of Public Prosecutions or counsel instructed by either for that purpose`
       AND `the proceedings are in respect of an offence for which he or she has the power to commence or to conduct a proceeding`
       AND `the proceedings have not been instituted by an Attorney General`
       AND `judgment has not been rendered`
       AND `the Attorney General of the province in which the proceedings are taken has not intervened`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may intervene in proceedings in the following circumstances: (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; and (d) ..." [F:may-if]

-- (2): sections 579 and 579.01 apply, with any modifications the circumstances require, to proceedings in which the Attorney General of Canada or the Director intervenes under this section.
-- src:12588 | (2) Sections 579 and 579.01 apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to proceedings in which the Attorney General of Canada or the Director of Public Prosecutions intervenes under this section.
@ref s 579.1(2) (src:12588-12588)
GIVEN `the Attorney General of Canada or the Director of Public Prosecutions intervenes under section 579.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579.1(2) sections 579 and 579.01 apply to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General of Canada or the Director of Public Prosecutions intervenes under section 579.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to proceedings in which the Attorney General of Canada or the Director of Public Prosecutions intervenes under this section"

§ `Section 580 -- Form of indictment`

-- 580 "An indictment is sufficient if it is on paper and is in Form 4." Form 4 itself is a Form at the end of the Act (not in this range).
-- src:12590 | 580 An indictment is sufficient if it is on paper and is in Form 4.
@ref s 580 (src:12590-12590)
GIVEN `the indictment is on paper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indictment is in Form 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 580 the indictment is sufficient` MEANS
    IF `the indictment is on paper` AND `the indictment is in Form 4`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An indictment is sufficient if it is on paper and is in Form 4" [M-a]
